  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "AI Agency — typographic index; Revenue OS — revenue control-room (A only)",
    "overview": "The approved C world uses dense Montserrat lettering, large uninterrupted color fields and sharply cut geometric letterforms. The visual tone is assertive and editorial; information is organized by type, space and color rather than floating boxes.\n\nThe current identity is LeadGenBureau. Russian copy and honest readiness labels remain legible parts of the composition. The visual system does not imply a unified production platform or verified commercial results.\n\nA is an independent Revenue OS world at `/revenue-os/`: daylight reading ground, midnight focused workspace and precise cobalt controls. Its control-room metaphor exposes a contact, risk and proposed next action without implying a live integrated platform. It shares the self-hosted Montserrat font and confirmed product facts with C, not C's visual composition.\n\n`src/main.tsx` dynamically imports `RevenueApp` with `revenue.css` for A and `App` with `styles.css` for C at `/`. Each entry has its own global styles; never load both stylesheets into one rendered page. All unprefixed frontmatter tokens and the incumbent prose describe C; all `a-` tokens and Revenue OS subsections describe A. The preserved C records are in `.impeccable/archive/concept-c/`.\n\nA follows the approved delegated composition `.impeccable/mocks/revenue-os/command.png`. The owner's later screenshot correction overrides its ambiguous long connector: a short downward SVG now connects the situation table to the recommendation in normal flow at every width. Review images, if present at `.impeccable/review/revenue-os/desktop.png` and `mobile.png`, are evidence rather than application assets. No raster is shipped; the only bundled visual asset is Montserrat with its license. The CLI font-ranking browser resolution failed; Montserrat is an intentional comp match, not a passed font-ranking result. No separate Revenue OS quality bar is established.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat plum, violet, cobalt and paper fields.",
      "Dense grotesque typography with tightly tracked headings.",
      "Square controls and containers; rounded readiness labels.",
      "A continuous geometric product index with readable text beneath its artwork.",
      "Daylight page and dark focused console.",
      "Geometric Montserrat display with fine rules and structured table content.",
      "Cobalt native controls, a connected stage path and textual readiness with three distinct dots.",
      "Local demonstration and draft preparation with explicit limits."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Field Identity Rule",
        "body": "Keep product-field colors paired with their demonstration panels; do not make readiness depend on color alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Display Exception Rule",
        "body": "Preserve the approved oversized hero on this surface; use the bounded section-heading ramp for ordinary extensions.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Field Rule",
        "body": "Preserve solid field separation and do not add floating shadows to the existing components.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Focused Console Rule",
        "body": "In A, Midnight identifies the demonstration or approach context; white surfaces carry the contact and recommendation inside it.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do retain solid fields, square controls and the bundled Montserrat family.",
      "Do keep readable product names and readiness text separate from geometric artwork.",
      "Do retain visible focus and the reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do use the existing mobile stacking and two-column index rather than shrinking desktop controls indefinitely.",
      "Do keep A's daylight reading ground, focused dark console and cobalt selected/action states scoped to its entry.",
      "Do preserve the text accompanying every readiness dot, risk marker and stage selection.",
      "Do retain native semantic controls, visible context-aware focus and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn the pinned hero sizing and compression into a default for every heading.",
      "Don't replace this flat geometric world with robots, neon gradients or volumetric illustrations.",
      "Don't reuse scenario text, synthetic data or readiness colors as proof of real results.",
      "Don't serve review evidence or mock images as application content.",
      "Don't load the two concepts' global styles together or extend C's compressed display and square fields into A.",
      "Don't present the synthetic workspace, local reveal or draft preview as integration, task creation or message delivery.",
      "Don't publish review images as application content or claim the failed font-ranking run passed."
    ]
  }
